# Cloudflare Turnstile keys for the /contact form.
# Create a widget at https://dash.cloudflare.com > Turnstile that allows both
# antoniorossi.net and www.antoniorossi.net, then set both values in Netlify under
# Site configuration > Environment variables and trigger a new deploy.
# The site key is inlined when the site builds, so it needs the Builds scope, and a
# production build fails without it. The secret is read by the Netlify function on
# each request, so it needs the Functions scope.
#
# Leave them unset locally: dev, preview and CI builds fall back to Cloudflare's test
# keys, which always pass, and `npm run dev` skips the Netlify Forms hand-off.
PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
